      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I have the answer. The wiki\u0027s \u0060[[credential-scoping]]\u0060 page directly addresses your question.\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through credential scoping:**\n\nThe key mechanism is that a **local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup** and **injects it only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process**, immediately before that process starts. Crucially, **the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the Anthropic API key simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent as well: it receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, not inherited from the Hub.\n\nSource: [[credential-scoping]]",
